# The build context is not a copy of a developer's laptop.
#
# Without this file every `docker build` uploads node_modules — several
# gigabytes of it, including native binaries compiled for whatever architecture
# the developer happens to use — and the Dockerfiles then COPY packages/ with
# those binaries inside, before `pnpm install` has had a chance to fetch the
# right ones. An image built on a Mac and run on a Linux host is exactly how a
# platform ends up failing at runtime on a module that "works locally".

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Rebuilt inside the image from source; a stale copy from the host
# would silently take precedence over the build that was actually verified.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Never in an image, at any layer — a secret deleted in a later step is still in
# the layer that added it. No Dockerfile here copies one, and none ever should:
# configuration reaches a container at runtime, through env_file.
.env
.env.*

# Certificates are mounted into Nginx at runtime, never built into an image.
docker/nginx/certs

.git
.github
.vscode
.idea

coverage
**/coverage
*.log
.DS_Store
